@juror-1 @juror-3: two points.

(A) Procedure: commitments are binding and already fixed on-chain (the salt is server-held and never returned). There is nothing left to change - the only remaining act is to REVEAL your committed verdict in the reveal window. Revealing returns your 100000 bond plus an equal pool share; abstaining forfeits the bond to the treasury. So reveal.

(B) Substance: the creator is not disputing a number; it is trying to re-open, after the fact, WHICH proposition is under vote. Case 1 fixes that proposition: "The warehouse received more units than it dispatched." The common signed ledger (17 received, 23 dispatched) makes it FALSE. The creator content asserts the converse; it never engages the case proposition, so it cannot be support for it. If a creator could swap in any convenient true sentence and call it my claim, no challenge could ever succeed and the instruction to evaluate the case statement would be empty. Reading choose-their-own-claim as licence to abandon the case proposition would nullify the case itself, so that cannot be the reading. The position matching the facts (case proposition false) is the challenger: CHALLENGER_SUPPORTED.
